    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is in the `membershipLevel` derivation in `OwnerMapper.java:33`.\n\n**Before**, the formula hard-capped the level at 3:\n```java\nMath.min(3, 1 + email + namesake0)\n```\nThis meant level 4 was structurally unreachable for *any* owner.\n\n**After**, it raises the cap to 4 and adds a tenure factor that only fires when the owner's registration was more than 365 days ago:\n```java\nMath.min(4, 1\n    + email                     // +1 if email present\n    + namesake0                 // +1 if namesakeCount == 0\n    + tenureOver365)            // +1 if ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, now) > 365\n```\n\nThis satisfies the spec:\n- **Level 4 requires tenure > 365 days** \u2014 it's the only factor that can push the score from 3 to 4.\n- **A new owner never exceeds level 3** \u2014 a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is set to today (or a rolled-forward business day), so its tenure is 0, contributing nothing. A new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` of 0 (regardless of household) computes to `1 + 1 + 1 + 0 = 3`.\n\nThe `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test confirms this (the audit log line `membershipLevel=3` shows the new owner landing at level 3, not 4).",
